	(text "U3 (eFuse B) does the same for the supply from the USB connector of the controller\nmodule: same thresholds (R5, R6), limit 0.76 A (0.67 A to 0.85 A, R13), fastest ramp,\nturn-on delay about 0.08 ms typical. R17 defines VBUS_P while U3 is off.\nR14, C5: position for a damper of VBUS_P, not fitted. Fit 0.33 ohm and 10 uF if the\nbench shows VBUS_P above 6.0 V when the data cable is plugged again.\nU5 drives +5V from USB-C (VBUS_CP) while PR1 is above 1.0 V, that is while VBUS_CP is\nabove 2.37 V (2.15 V to 2.59 V, calculated from R18, R19), otherwise from the module\n(VBUS_P). It blocks reverse current into both inputs. C8 delays PR1 by 0.19 ms, until\nthe ramp of U4 is nearly complete.\nOrder of the thresholds on a falling rail: supervisor of +5V 3.83 V to 4.00 V (next\nsheet), eFuse off 2.67 V to 2.87 V, change of source 2.15 V to 2.59 V. The multiplexer\nleaves USB-C only when U4 is already off.\nSRC_ST (TP5): open = USB-C in use, low = supply of the module in use."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 162.56 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "57af5429-fdc1-56d9-a76f-52d9abaf8549")
	)
	(text "J2 is a USB-C sink for 5 V. R7 and R11 pull CC1 and CC2 down; the firmware reads the CC\nvoltage through the monitor converter: below 0.61 V default USB, 0.70 V to 1.16 V 1.5 A,\n1.31 V to 2.04 V 3 A. U2 protects the CC pins; D2, C2 and C3 sit at the receptacle,\nahead of the current limit. D2 stands off 10 V: the input tolerates no more than that.\nU4 (eFuse A) turns on when VBUS_C is above 2.92 V to 3.09 V and off below 2.67 V to 2.87 V\n(R9, R10, which also bleed VBUS_C). It limits the current to 2.0 A (1.81 A to 2.17 A,\nR15) and clamps its output to 5.28 V to 5.61 V when the input is above 5.54 V to 5.83 V\n(R12). C4 sets a turn-on delay of about 0.25 ms and a ramp of 13 V/ms (datasheet, typical).\nTP3 shows the input current, 0.297 V per ampere, behind R16.\nR20, C9 and C10 damp the ring of a contact that closes; D4 takes their charge back\nto the input when the plug is pulled, so that the output stays within 0.3 V of the input."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 20.32 15.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "76346e9a-a10b-569a-8193-fd3c41c7f22f")
	)
